{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>You are children to HaShem your Elohim; you shall not gash yourselves.</b> For it is not fitting to show the ultimate degree of grief and sorrow over a deceased relative when there remains a relative superior to him in rank and in hope of good. Therefore, you are children of HaShem, who is your Father, existing forever — it is not fitting that you grieve and mourn to the uttermost over any dead person." "<b>Nor shall you make a bald spot between your eyes for the dead, for you are a holy people.</b> And likewise one should not be greatly distressed over the harm that befalls the dead person in his death, for you are a holy people destined for the life of the World to Come, in which the life of the spirit is better than all the life of this world."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:25.668320573Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}